On Sun, Jun 17, 2012 at 9:49 AM, Escape Landsome <escaaape@gmail.com> wrote:

> And, another thing : you will never need to define "cinkyfalte"
> because cinkyfalte can be the fact that a lion hunts, the fact that
> people hunt lions, and even the fact that people hunts using lions as
> if they were hunting hounds, or the fact that lions are used a arrows
> to hunt birds (!!???)
>
> And the fact that it is more likely the first or second instance than
> the third or the fourth comes not from a dictionary structure, but
> from enclyclopedic wisdom
>

That statement is patently false. All Lojbanic words can only have one
meaning. While this meaning can and usually is rather vague, a hunting lion
and hunting using a lion are different concepts and therefore must be two
different words. It is therefore necessary to define which is meant.

